ger additions were required outcome verification; the interruption test used an isolated temporary directory that was removed; and the reboot was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol. Post-execution observations show no failed services, healthy package state, no unexpected persistent temporary artifacts, and no meaningful new network exposure. The restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, acknowledgement, a different post-restart boot ID, and recovered script, data, ledger, and system state were all directly captured.","evidence_ids":["cmd-89f5a3bc058141b3","cmd-36f0cb9c38ad46e1","cmd-d4def61787f24085","cmd-88463c1e36ae4258","cmd-c96fd87495cf4708","cmd-835508a968ea4aa3","cmd-e6079391f08046dd","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. Concurrent ownership, exactly-once ledger results, interruption recovery, preservation across restart, and OS/kernel compatibility were demonstrated. The mandatory node-restart evidence is coherent and independently corroborated by the lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":[]}
